# mix-of-capabilities 04×12 — il nesso causale letto nel verso della conversa.
# «Most outbreaks result from poorly maintained cooling towers» (Legionella,
# Wikipedia) si leggeva `result(outbreaks, towers)`: la causa c'era, in un cassetto
# che nessuna domanda causale apre. `converse_particle_reading(result, from,
# causes)` (grammar.p0) fa leggere lo schema «@O result from @S» come `causes/2`.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the read converse becomes a cause and answers the causal question]
!timeout 30
> most legionella outbreaks result from poorly maintained cooling towers
<~ poorly maintained cooling towers
!query causes(poorly_maintained_cooling_towers, legionella_outbreaks)
!query! result(legionella_outbreaks, $Y)
!query attenuated_reading(most, $S)
> what causes legionella outbreaks?
<~ poorly maintained cooling towers
